[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6230079868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124196#issuecomment-6230079868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124196","id":6230079868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABc1d5fA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-17T05:18:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T05:36:40Z","body":"This appears to be a regression caused by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123072; testing just before that commit, my mouse's scroll wheel works as expected, but testing on the merge commit, it takes the large steps.\n\nLooking further into the code and modifying it a bit, I see that changing line 925 on `godot_content_view.mm` from\n```objc\n[self processScrollEvent:event button:(0 < delta_y ? MouseButton::WHEEL_UP : MouseButton::WHEEL_DOWN) factor:delta_y_abs];\n```\nto\n```objc\n[self processScrollEvent:event button:(0 < delta_y ? MouseButton::WHEEL_UP : MouseButton::WHEEL_DOWN) factor:(delta_y_abs * 0.009)];\n```\n(matching the net result of the old multiplications above) does fix the issue _when using the mouse_. I've not tested it with a trackpad but given the nature of the change, I would expect it to make the trackpad feel like a very slow crawl 😅\n\nSecondly, the mouse (again, a Logitech MX Master 3S) is apparently providing the \"precise scrolling delta\" data, i.e., it's triggering\n```objc\nif ([event hasPreciseScrollingDeltas]) {\n\tdelta_x = [event scrollingDeltaX];\n\tdelta_y = [event scrollingDeltaY];\n}\n```\nAnd, a single \"click\" on the scroll wheel is giving me a `delta_y` of about `13.0`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6230079868/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6239931116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124196#issuecomment-6239931116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124196","id":6239931116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABc-3K7A","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-17T19:49:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T19:49:36Z","body":"I have a Logitech MX Anywhere 3 and the scroll wheel works fine in both ratchet mode and free-spin mode. \n\nAre you using any additional configuration software with the mouse?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6239931116/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6239958578","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124196#issuecomment-6239958578","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124196","id":6239958578,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABc-42Mg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-17T19:51:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T19:52:23Z","body":"I do have Logi Options+ installed on my computer (mouse configuration software that Logitech suggests installing when using the MX Master mice). It sounded like people on some other issues may have found that uninstalling that program fixed the problem for them, so I'll give it a try myself soon as well and report back on the results.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6239958578/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6240007807","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124196#issuecomment-6240007807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124196","id":6240007807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABc-72fw","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-17T19:55:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T19:55:39Z","body":"I'm finding that the scrolling in Godot is now very similar to Safari. I scroll the wheel slowly, it moves a few pixel rows at a time (in both Safari and Godot), but as I increase the acceleration, it moves faster. \n\nAs an aside, it feels very different, having used a track pad for over a decade as my main driver for scrolling.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6240007807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6244855209","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124196#issuecomment-6244855209","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124196","id":6244855209,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdDjtqQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-18T02:44:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T02:44:45Z","body":"Uninstalling Logi Options+ appears to have fixed the issue of single \"clicks\" (\"ratchets\"?) jumping too far in a scroll view! So fortunately for contributors but unfortunately for users, it seems like the ball must be largely in Logitech's court now 😅\n\nThe momentum in the script editor feels like it goes a bit farther than I'd like, so perhaps it could be good for us to introduce a \"friction\" setting...? Perhaps I should try it with the Magic Trackpad and see how it feels there.\n\nOverall, given that there are probably a fair number of people using mice instead of trackpads on Macs, and as far as I know the MX Master series is considered one of the high-end/technical options, it'd probably be good for us to have some kind of way to have MX Master-friendly scroll behavior.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6244855209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6284521885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124196#issuecomment-6284521885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124196","id":6284521885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdpYxnQ","user":{"login":"shakesoda","id":219510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTUxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda","html_url":"https://github.com/shakesoda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shakesoda/r